Good call, and thanks for the failing list. The linter was doing two real jobs after all, both now moved into the generators:

- Template glitches the fixer used to paper over: indented `<?php` control tags in the webhook `RequestParser` (they leaked their leading whitespace into the generated code), the schedule placeholder indent, missing blank lines in the Voter template, docblock/comment indentation and a trailing comma in the custom Authenticator.
- One functional leftover: `make:serializer:normalizer` always added `use App\Entity\X;` even when the entity does not exist, and relied on `no_unused_imports` to clean it up. The use statement is now only added when the entity exists.

@kbond so mostly fluff, with those exceptions: the raw PHP-Parser output was already properly indented (the `ClassSourceManipulator` fixtures in `tests/Util/fixtures/` never went through the fixer), what it really covered was template typos and that unused import. No one-liner methods, promise.

The remaining CI red matches what already fails on the `1.x` nightlies (MakeController invoke, MakeForm relations, serializer-encoder legacy, Panther). Schedule, Voter, Webhook, Normalizer and Authenticator suites pass locally now.

