by Amoifr at 2026-08-18T08:07:08Z

The Yaml failures are pre-existing: the same four data sets fail on the `1.x` nightlies (e.g. run 32084125012, same job), they come from a symfony/yaml formatting change for sequences of maps. I can send a separate PR for those if you want.

On keeping php-cs-fixer in the tests: I like it as a safety net against template drift, now that nothing repairs the output at runtime. Concrete shape I would propose:

- keep the userland ruleset as a test fixture (basically the removed `config/php-cs-fixer.config.php`);
- after a maker runs in a functional test, run the fixer once in dry-run over the generated files (the harness knows them), through `tools/php-cs-fixer` which CI already installs, and fail with the diff;
- once per generated app keeps the cost to one process per test instead of one per file; going fully programmatic through the Runner API can come later if that is still too slow.

Want it in this PR or as a follow-up? Happy either way.
